  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Thrift: Fix fallback when subdissector fails",
  "description": "- Ensure all sub-dissector errors use THRIFT_SUBDISSECTOR_ERROR instead\n  of THRIFT_REQUEST_REASSEMBLY to effectively fallback.\n- Reset proto_depth before fallback on generic dissector.\n\nNote 1: The issue was seen at the same time as !16361 but avoiding the need to fallback was more critical than fixing the fallback itself. I did most of the development by reverting the previous patch but it is also visible using a very low value for `thrift.nested_type_depth` (Value of 5 shows 3 occurrences of fallback in the armeria capture, see !16361).\n\nNote 2: The issue exists since 4.2 and the patch can be applied on the 4.2 and 4.4 branches (fuzzing have been running on 4.4 for a few hours now) so it would be good to apply it as well for current sub-dissectors using the stable 4.4 version (4.2 can be done upon request only as most people would upgrade to 4.4). Thanks.",
